  "energy_share_ratio_a_b": "r_k = ln( s_k(model) / s_k(Dense teacher) ), s_k = band-k energy share on Ω_T (TPV: local energy attribution of the full-plane band decomposition to Ω_T cells; channels pooled); plotted as r_k / ln 2",
  "real_pseudo_c_d": "per band, cross-fitted ridge regression of the student band-k field from the Dense-teacher band-k field: outer 2-fold split by alternating 60° φ sectors, inner leave-one-sector-out choice of the ridge parameter from {1e-3, 1e-2, 1e-1, 1, 10, 100, 1000} × tr(XᵀX)/C, R² relative to the training-half mean. real_k = clip(R²(S_k←T_k), 0, 1) × student band-k energy share; pseudo_k = remainder. Both are divided per frame by the band-k energy share of the re-truncated teacher (its real + pseudo), then the median over frames is taken. Real energy is a lower bound and pseudo an upper bound (only same-band linear relations count). The grey segment is the same quantity for the re-truncated teacher (what the teacher itself reproduces).",
  "paired_e_f": "per frame (LiEqualizer − LiSeer) of real (resp. pseudo) energy ÷ the same denominator, median over frames",
  "null_flag": "† marks bands where the cross-scene null (student frame f vs. teacher frame g, 13 pairs) median R²(S←T) exceeds 0.05 for either student",
